Implement user story SKY-002-impl: Implement SkyscannerClient class and typed interfaces

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.ts with the SkyscannerClient class, SearchParams and FlightResult interfaces, global-fetch-based searchFlights method, apiKey validation, HTTP error handling, parse error handling, and opt-in mock mode driven by MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API env var.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/skyscanner/client.ts exports SkyscannerClient class, SearchParams interface { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number }, and FlightResult interface { price: number; currency: string; airline: string; departure: string; arrival: string; duration: number; stops: number }
- SkyscannerClient constructor accepts { apiKey?: string }; uses explicit apiKey if provided, falls back to RAPIDAPI_KEY env var if omitted; throws a descriptive Error (e.g. 'Skyscanner API key is required: pass apiKey or set RAPIDAPI_KEY') when neither is present or when the resolved key is an empty string
- searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]> uses the Node.js 18+ global fetch exclusively — no third-party HTTP library imported
- searchFlights rejects with an Error whose message includes the HTTP status code (e.g. 'Skyscanner API error: 429') on any 4xx or 5xx response; the apiKey value must NOT appear in the error message
- searchFlights rejects with a descriptive parse Error (e.g. 'Invalid Skyscanner response shape') when the response body does not match the expected FlightResult[] structure
- Mock mode: when process.env.MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true' (exact string match), searchFlights returns a deterministic FlightResult[] fixture without invoking fetch at all; when the env var is unset, empty, or any value other than 'true', searchFlights performs a real fetch call — no silent fallback to mock data on real-call failure
- tsc --noEmit exits 0 on src/skyscanner/client.ts with no type errors





